{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.HyperellipticZ5Classification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.HyperellipticZ5Classification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Parity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.X5Classification.minimal_z5_branch_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.X5Classification.minimal_z5_branch_size","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/hyperelliptic-z5-classification.lean#L34-L55","doc":"**Arithmetic core of the classification**:\nthe smallest even integer ≥ 4 that is an admissible `C_5`-invariant\nbranch-set size is `6`.  This is the Diophantine content of the\nRiemann–Hurwitz argument forcing minimal genus to `g = 2`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:hyperelliptic-z5-classification}`\nRef: [bolza1887] https://doi.org/10.2307/2369402 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.X5Classification.AdmissibleBranchSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.X5Classification.AdmissibleBranchSize","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/hyperelliptic-z5-classification.lean#L26-L32","doc":"The admissible sizes of a `C_5`-invariant subset of `ℙ¹(ℂ)`:\nnon-negative combinations `a·5 + b·1` where `a ≥ 0` counts\nsize-5 generic orbits and `b ∈ {0, 1, 2}` counts fixed-point\ncontributions (the two fixed points of `x ↦ ζ₅·x` on `ℙ¹`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}